<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 8.818 percent at Monday's auction from 8.830 percent at the previous auction on July 7.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 774.950 million pounds, replace bills worth 709.575 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 700 million pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Jan 13, 1998 (Jan 06, 1998)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.818 percent (8.830)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 774.950 million (894.950 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,028.800 million (1,266.125 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.480-8.899 percent (8.574-8.889)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.480-10.200 percent (8.574-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 69 (65)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 87 (104)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
